        "@id": "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference/REF-672B9D6A479F"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "Source reports this apparatus type in its manufacturing or characterization workflow. Atomized salt precursors become refractory-metal oxide nanoparticles, which are charged, mobility-selected and collected. TSI9302 atomizer,3077 charge neutralizer and3085 DMA are explicitly named. Reduction produces metal catalysts for substrate CVD or floating-catalyst CVD SWCNT growth. TSI3756 condensation particle counter measures aerosol concentrations. Unnamed furnace and collection assemblies must remain class-level."
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#relation": [
      {
        "@value": "supports_claim"
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#reviewStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "claim_checked"
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#scope": [
      {
        "@value": "Registry issue date is2020-10-02; electronic article/JATS date is2020-09-30. Existing P21 is laser cold-wall CVD; P26 specifically robot-assisted arrays. Neither should inherit this entire recipe as exact source support. M-class placement is curator interpretation; no unnamed commercial model is validated."
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#sourceLocator": [
      {
        "@value": "Materials and Methods > NP synthesis, size selection, and collection; CNT growth on substrate and FCCVD growth; Aerosol characterization, AFM, HRTEM, ED, XRD, and Raman mapping (JATS sec11–sec14)"
      }
    ]
  },
