      {
        "@value": "Source reports this apparatus type in its manufacturing or characterization workflow. Electrospinning a hydroxyapatite/PAN precursor followed by nitrogen-atmosphere carbonization produces hydroxyapatite-containing carbon nanofibers. The BTF-1200C vacuum tube furnace is expressly named. Further preparation incorporates myoglobin and Nafion into an electrode coating. The electrospinner is not identified by make/model."
      }
    ],
