        "@id": "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference/REF-85D684544148"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "Repeated phosphorus insertion and oxidative extraction converts Pd seed nanocrystals to hollow Pd nanoshells. The authors describe heated magnetic stirring, centrifugation/washing and unspecified sonication. Repeating the conversion enlarges voids and thins shells. Atmosphere and temperature alter the observed morphology; this is a reported study result, not an app prediction."
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#relation": [
      {
        "@value": "supports_claim"
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#reviewStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "claim_checked"
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#scope": [
      {
        "@value": "No named manufacturing maker/model; do not create a commercial instrument identity. Sonication does not resolve probe versus bath; do not claim either exact model. Three-neck flask and nitrogen flow do not independently establish a Schlenk manifold. Named TEM, XRD, ICP-MS and electrochemical apparatus are characterization/catalytic testing, separate from manufacture. One published source used two atomistic and experimental analyses; not independent validation of app predictions. P-class maps the stated source stage, not all alternative ontology steps."
      }
    ],
    "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#sourceLocator": [
      {
        "@value": "Methods / Synthesis of Pd nanocubes; Methods / Synthesis of hollow Pd nanocrystals"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/reference-link/LINK-SW17-C1D9E7904188",
    "@type": [
      "https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#ReferenceLink"
